menu "LagunBus — output"

config LAGUN_TWAI_TX
    int "TWAI transmit GPIO"
    default 4
    help
        4 and 5 by default, because on the ESP32-C3 Super Mini they are broken out
        and play no other role. AVOID 2, 8 and 9 — those are boot-mode strapping
        pins, and their state at reset decides whether the board starts at all.
        Avoid 18 and 19 too: USB Serial/JTAG goes that way, that is, flashing and
        the log.

config LAGUN_TWAI_RX
    int "TWAI receive GPIO"
    default 5

config LAGUN_RELAY_GPIO
    int "Relay GPIO"
    default 10
    help
        A relay module driven by a LOW level has `Invert` set in the endpoint's
        attributes. Check yours — the mistake shows as a relay switched on the
        whole time except for the moment it is meant to be on.

config LAGUN_LED_GPIO
    int "On-board LED GPIO (-1 = none)"
    default 8
    help
        On the Super Mini the LED sits on GPIO8 and lights on a low level. It is a
        boot-mode strapping pin, but after boot it may be used as an output.

config LAGUN_BITRATE
    int "Bus speed [bit/s]"
    default 500000
    help
        Has to agree with the hub and with EVERY other node. A node at a different
        speed not only hears nobody — it corrupts frames for all the others.

endmenu
